\b Eyal Espresso Firmware Revision History\b0\par
\par
\b Current Version\b0\par
0.4.12\par
\par
\b Latest Version Feature List\b0\par
- System constants and profiles are now split into separate embedded files (`SystemConstants.xml` and `Profiles.xml`), with independent parsing paths and profile-count validation sourced from `Profiles.xml`.\par
- Settings now uses button-only actions: Target Temperature and Preinfusion sliders were removed, `System Constants` now shows only global constants, and a new `View Profiles` action opens the recursive profile viewer separately.\par
- Client dataset bootstrap now requires a complete profile set payload and rejects partial profile datasets; TF dataset persistence removes stale prior files before rewrite.\par
- Live Shot keeps the full 50 Hz timeline aligned to T=0 by latching session start from the first packet elapsed-time sample and replaying the full frozen shot window with corrected end-of-shot axis scaling.\par
- Plot-range autoscale toggles and manual Y-axis limits now reload from persisted system constants so checkbox state and ranges survive rebuilds and power cycles.\par
- Brew-page shot progress now resets to `0s` and `0.0 g` after brew completion while preserving the profile expected-time and target context in labels.\par
- Plot history depth is increased to 2200 points to retain longer 50 Hz sessions without clipping the full-shot replay.\par
- Protocol bootstrap now supports full LCD dataset ingestion (`settings` + full profile structs), applies it to runtime constants, and persists the dataset snapshot to TF for reboot reload.\par
- System Constants UI now uses a tabbed viewer with a legacy-compatible summary tab plus a recursive `Profiles Tree` tab that exposes all dataset fields.\par
- Live Shot packet ingestion now processes multi-sample packets at 5 samples per 100 ms, and communication snapshot text capacity is expanded to carry full dataset payload events safely.\par
- System constants defaults/XML now define five brew profiles, and monitor capture post-check now verifies COM availability before conditional release attempts.\par
- Live Shot axis labels now stay pinned to valid chart geometry across tab changes, use dynamic grid-aligned X-label placement, and show expected brew time next to the active profile name.\par
- Live Shot rendering now guards against non-finite pressure/flow/weight/temperature/time samples by reusing the last valid values so traces no longer disappear.\par
- README now formalizes the cross-project MUST governance rule for `Client FW`, `Server FW`, and `Server Simulator` version lines.\par
- Live Shot plotting now starts from T=0, keeps X-axis labels aligned to the grid, preserves full shot-duration visibility, and improves flow/weight continuity when incoming samples are sparse or invalid.\par
- Keepalive duplicate handling now replays the cached correlated response for duplicate request IDs instead of single-shot no-resend behavior.\par
- Wi-Fi power-save policy is now dynamic: initialization and backlight ON force `WIFI_PS_NONE`, while backlight OFF applies `WIFI_PS_MIN_MODEM` to save power when the screen is dark.\par
- Monitor capture workflow is now explicitly standardized to `scripts/monitor_capture.ps1` with pre/post COM availability checks, busy-port release attempts, and post-capture release verification.\par
- README approval-bootstrap guidance now requires scoped executable approvals for known workspace tools under `C:/Espressif/Eyal_Projects_ESP32_S3/...` paths and explicitly forbids blanket arbitrary `.exe` approvals.\par
- Minor version release checkpoint: promoted client version line to 0.4.0 for the synchronized dual-project release.\par
- Simulate Data graph now updates per packet with labeled X/Y axes, packet/sample timing display, stream idle auto-sync, and stop-action FIFO+plot reset behavior.\par
- Downlink Simulate Data FIFO now prefers delayed processing over packet drops, with larger queue depth and live backlog telemetry (`RX_FIFO_PacketBacklogNPackets`).\par
- Build/flash workflow scripts now enforce COM release before and after build, flash, and monitor operations, aligned with the documented rule-gated sequence.\par
- Simulate Data toggle now mirrors backend DataSimulationOn/DataSimulationOFF events in real time, including resilient text-event synchronization in the client communication snapshot.\par
- ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-4.3b-Box hardware initialization (RGB LCD + GT911 touch).\par
- LVGL 9.x display and input integration.\par
- Demo-based LVGL porting layer imported from `08_lvgl_Porting` and adapted to project layout.\par
- Demo-style RGB panel timing/alignment fields applied in hardware initialization.\par
- Basic Brew Control UI with on-screen toggle and state label.\par
- Build/flash workflow helper with commit + sub-version prompt.\par
- Project migrated from devcontainer workflow to local ESP-IDF workflow.\par
- Stable RGB display recipe validated for the first UI-stable release.\par
- Dark tab-based UI with swipe-left and swipe-right page navigation.\par
- Dedicated requirements and design document template added to the repository.\par
- TF card initialization and mount verification added to normal startup.\par
- Initialization splash screen added before the main workflow UI appears.\par
- RTC initialization added at startup using the current firmware build timestamp.\par
- TF card startup path corrected so mount and file read verification succeed on the Waveshare board.\par
- Wi-Fi station initialization and access-point scan test added to normal startup.\par
- Flash layout updated to match the board's 16MB device and provide a 7MB factory app partition.\par
- Settings-page backlight control added through CH422G with touch-to-wake recovery.\par
- Automatic backlight-off after 30 seconds without touch added with 1-second timer resolution.\par
- All workflow text and controls moved fully inside the tab area, with a persistent bottom clock bar occupying the lower 10% of the display.\par
- Press and toggle controls updated to use button-style surfaces with pressed/check-state colors and press in/out animation.\par
- RTC startup now preserves valid retained time instead of overwriting it unconditionally on every boot.\par
- Settings tab now includes a `Set Clock` flow with rollers for day, month, year, hour, and minute plus a `Done` action that writes the selected time to the RTC.\par
- Windows monitoring workflow now includes a fallback raw serial capture helper and separate flash/monitor tasks when `idf.py monitor` fails on this host.\par
- Bottom clock bar now uses a larger font and full date-time format with weekday, month, day, year, and seconds.\par
- Settings page now includes a symmetric two-column action layout and a `Connection Info` overlay with live IP/port/telemetry text.\par
- Connection Info now includes a `Reset Connection` action backed by a dedicated low-level Wi-Fi/TCP communication state machine with default server settings and live runtime status.\par
- Connection Info now includes a `Scan for Devices` action backed by a dedicated 10-second Wi-Fi discovery workflow, plus a hardened serial monitor capture helper that releases COM ports cleanly after log capture.\par
- Wi-Fi hardware bring-up is now working from the low-level communication path, including lazy driver initialization before reset/connect and scan operations.\par
- Connection Info reset/scan crashes caused by `comm_link` stack overflow are fixed by increasing task stack budget and moving scan AP-record buffers off the task stack.\par
- Connection Info reset now drives the framed low-level transport reset flow, and the client transport topology now matches the server-side `reset -> initialize -> connect -> keepalive -> send_data -> error` sequence with shared CRC16 frame structure and richer runtime telemetry.\par
- Client low-level transport now reaches stable keepalive with the ESP32-C3 bridge, uses a larger guarded RX buffer, and supports reset-driven reconnect against bridge-side stale-session replacement.\par
- Sound helper scripts now launch tracked background playback/loop workers, store descriptive PID metadata under `.cache\sound_processes`, and the same helper set is duplicated into the `08_lvgl_Porting` demo project with its own local version file.\par
- Startup mode prompt now auto-selects Online after a 5-second visible countdown while carrying an explicit Offline placeholder flag through the staged initialization flow.\par
- RS485 controller probing now includes gated TX/RX diagnostics, and the wait-sound helpers now record append-only sound event logs while the build/flash prompt starts and stops wait playback around explicit user input waits.\par
- RS485/UART2 is now initialized only as future-ready hardware bring-up; startup no longer sends `INIT?` or `VER?`, and the peripheral background loop no longer emits RS485 heartbeat traffic.\par
- Client Wi-Fi reconnect during transport initialization now retries within the existing timeout window and no longer tears down a valid station/IP while association and DHCP are still settling after simulator reset.\par
- Client transport now uses `wait_for_com_reset` plus a latched `ConnectionFault` banner instead of a transport `error` state, and the low-level state flow/docs were updated around `reset -> initialize -> connect -> keepalive -> wait_for_com_reset`.\par
- Simulator-side transport alignment work is integrated into the client release baseline, including the offline-aware startup contract, RS485 startup disablement, and the current two-counter keepalive contract with `ServerLiveInteger` and `ClientLiveInteger`.\par
- Keepalive handling now preserves the client-side counter baseline across non-keepalive acknowledgements, so generic `ACK` frames no longer overwrite the live-integer snapshot between bridge keepalive exchanges.\par
- Communication keepalive supervision now uses session/request correlation with immediate frame parsing, duplicate-request handling without state bouncing, and a 300ms keepalive period that keeps the link in `KEEPALIVE` without rapid reconnect loops.\par
- Connection Info now includes an `Auto Reconnect` toggle that defaults ON and controls whether retry-limit exhaustion auto-restarts the connect path.\par
- Connection fault latching now occurs at the third keepalive timeout window and clears only after re-entering `KEEPALIVE`, with Wi-Fi and TCP default timeout windows reduced to 1000 ms.\par
- TopLayer keepalive flow is now explicitly split into `KeepAliveServerReceive` and `KeepAliveClientSend`, with one response per accepted request and parity checks to keep server values even and client values odd.\par
- Reset now fast-paths directly to `connect` when low-layer Wi-Fi is still healthy, reducing reconnect latency after reset retries.\par
\par
\b X=0, Y=4\b0\par
\b 2026-04-03 22:40:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.4.12\par
- Summary: Split system constants/profile sources and viewers, tightened full-profile bootstrap validation, and formalized flash-only wrapper behavior.\par
- Notes: `main/CMakeLists.txt` now embeds both `SystemConstants.xml` and `Profiles.xml`; `main/system_constants.*` now parses globals from `SystemConstants.xml` and profiles from `Profiles.xml`, and removes stale TF dataset files before rewrite. `main/communication/ProtocolLCD_Controller.c` now requires full fixed-size profile datasets during bootstrap and marks dataset sync only after full-structure validation. `main/ui_screen.c` now provides separate Settings overlays for `System Constants` and `View Profiles`, and removes Target Temperature/Preinfusion sliders to keep Settings button-only. `scripts/idfw.cmd`, `README.md`, and `AGENTS.md` now support and document explicit `flash`/`flash-only` versus `build flash` flow selection.\par
\par
\b 2026-04-03 18:15:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.4.11\par
- Summary: Fixed Live Shot session-time anchoring and persisted plot-range UI state while extending 50 Hz history coverage for full-shot replay.\par
- Notes: `main/ui_screen.c` now stores `plot_session_start_time_s`, anchors realtime samples to explicit brew elapsed time, keeps a fixed 20 ms sample delta for 5-sample packets, and recomputes non-rolling end-of-shot axis span from the full captured timeline. UI plot settings now reload from `system_constants` during page build so autoscale checkboxes and manual max values persist after reinit. Brew-shot progress display now resets to zero values when not actively brewing, while still showing the configured target and expected shot time context. History capacity was raised from 1200 to 2200 points for longer 50 Hz captures. `main/system_constants.c` now loads TF profile datasets before applying SD plot-range overrides so persisted user plot settings are not overwritten.\par
\par
\b 2026-04-02 22:27:44\b0\par
- Version: 0.4.10\par
- Summary: Added full LCD profile dataset bootstrap/persistence, expanded profile defaults/schema, and introduced a tabbed recursive System Constants viewer with packet-level multi-sample Live Shot ingestion.\par
- Notes: `main/communication/DataStructuresLCD_Controller.h` now defines EEPROM-mirrored dataset structs (`lcd_controller_settings_t`, `lcd_controller_profile_t`, `lcd_controller_dataset_t`) and protocol constants/events were extended in `main/communication/SystemStatesLCD_Controller.h`. `main/communication/ProtocolLCD_Controller.c` now requests `LCDProtoProfileDatasetGet` during bootstrap, parses profile dataset payloads, derives catalog data from datasets, and applies/persists datasets through `system_constants_apply_lcd_dataset(..., true)`. `main/system_constants.*` now seeds defaults for five profiles, stores/loads `LCDProfileDataset.bin` on TF, and exposes dataset access APIs. `main/SystemConstants.xml` profile count/defaults were expanded from three to five profiles. `main/ui_screen.c` now adds tabbed System Constants presentation (`Constants` + recursive `Profiles Tree`) and processes multi-sample brew packets (5 samples per 100 ms) during Live Shot plotting. `main/CommunicationFunctions.h` increased `last_received_text` capacity for long dataset text events, and `scripts/monitor_capture.ps1` now validates post-monitor COM availability before conditional release retries.\par
\par
\b 2026-04-01 16:53:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.4.9\par
- Summary: Stabilized Live Shot axis rendering through tab/layout transitions, hardened invalid-sample fallback behavior, and formalized cross-project version governance in README.\par
- Notes: `main/ui_screen.c` now caches the last valid chart geometry so custom axes and labels remain stable when the tab is hidden or layout briefly reports zero size, aligns X-axis labels directly under computed vertical grid positions, recomputes post-shot axis span/ticks so labels stay consistent through full-brew rendering, and falls back to the latest valid pressure/temperature/weight/flow/time values when incoming samples are non-finite or invalid. Header runtime text now appends expected brew time in `(<xx> S)` format beside the profile name. `README.md` now codifies the MUST cross-project version governance rule for client firmware, bridge firmware, and simulator version scopes.\par
\par
\b 2026-04-01 12:55:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.4.8\par
- Summary: Stabilized Live Shot plotting and keepalive duplicate recovery, added dynamic Wi-Fi power-save switching tied to backlight state, and hardened mandatory monitor-capture workflow.\par
- Notes: `main/ui_screen.c` now aligns plot X-axis labels to grid positions without `s` suffixes, tracks elapsed shot time from zero, extends non-rolling display to expected brew duration, improves flow/weight continuity with fallback estimation from weight deltas, moves Y-axis label groups rightward for plot-space efficiency, removes the temperature graph and its autoscale checkbox, and compacts the bottom controls to enlarge the chart area. `main/CommunicationFunctions.c` now replays cached keepalive responses when duplicate `req` IDs arrive, replacing the previous single-shot no-resend duplicate path. `main/peripherals_manager.c` and `main/hardware_init.*` now force `WIFI_PS_NONE` at Wi-Fi initialization and switch between `WIFI_PS_NONE` (backlight ON) and `WIFI_PS_MIN_MODEM` (backlight OFF) with explicit rollback comments for stability validation. `scripts/monitor_capture.ps1` now enforces pre-check/release/retry logic for busy COM ports and verifies release after capture, and `README.md` now mandates this script as the only approved monitor method.\par
\par
