\b 2026-03-23 17:20:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.3.7\par
- Summary: Improved Simulate Data graph fidelity/timing visibility, removed packet-loss behavior from RX FIFO handling, and hardened COM release behavior in build/flash/monitor tooling.\par
- Notes: `main/ui_screen.c` now keeps graph updates paced to packet arrival, auto-scales Y around waveform amplitude, renders explicit X/Y axis labels, shows packet/sample timing and `RX_FIFO_PacketBacklogNPackets`, places the Done action below the graph, and clears FIFO/plot when simulation stops. `main/data_payload.*` increased downlink FIFO depth and changed push semantics to wait for space instead of dropping packets. `scripts/idfw.cmd`, `scripts/idfw.ps1`, `scripts/flash_hidden.ps1`, `scripts/monitor_capture.ps1`, and `scripts/build_flash_prompt.sh` now release COM around tool actions to reduce stale-port lock failures.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-23 16:40:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.3.6\par
- Summary: Release checkpoint commit covering all current workspace updates and backend-aware Simulate Data toggle synchronization.\par
- Notes: The client now mirrors DataSimulationOn and DataSimulationOFF backend text events into the Simulate Data toggle state while preserving existing chart and packet-flow behavior.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-17 14:50:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.21\par
- Summary: Split client keepalive into explicit receive/send states, added reset fast-path behavior, and aligned top/bottom-layer docs to the implemented transport rules.\par
- Notes: `main/CommunicationFunctions.*` now runs the client TopLayer as `reset -> initialize -> connect -> keepalive_server_receive <-> keepalive_client_send -> error`, enforces single-response handling per keepalive request, and keeps retry escalation at 3-window timeout/3 bottom-layer retry thresholds with Auto Reconnect control. `docs/architecture/top_bottom_layer_state_machine.mmd` and `README.md` were updated to match the implemented behavior. Verified via successful build/flash cycles during COM4/COM9 transport debugging.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-16 16:53:49\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.20\par
- Summary: Added Auto Reconnect control, aligned fault-banner timing to the third keepalive timeout, and reduced retry timeout windows to 1 second.\par
- Notes: `main/ui_screen.c` now provides a Connection Info `Auto Reconnect` toggle and live ON/OFF telemetry. `main/CommunicationFunctions.*` now exposes runtime auto-reconnect policy control, auto-retries connect after bottom-layer retry exhaustion when enabled, and latches `ConnectionFault` at the third keepalive timeout window while clearing it only on successful `KEEPALIVE` re-entry. Default Wi-Fi and TCP timeout windows are now both 1000 ms to shorten retry latency. Verified with successful build and multiple successful flashes to `COM9`.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-16 14:52:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.19\par
- Summary: Stabilized client-side communication handshake and keepalive supervision for the bridge-owned session protocol.\par
- Notes: `main/CommunicationFunctions.c` now parses incoming frames immediately (no RX parse blocking window), tracks `sid` and `req` metadata in keepalive exchanges, ignores stale requests, handles duplicate keepalive requests without cycling back through interim-debug, and supervises the link with a single rolling 0.3-second deadline model. The default keepalive period was raised to 300ms for timing margin. Verified with successful build, successful flash to `COM9`, and monitor capture showing `Connect -> InterimDebug -> Keepalive` with sustained session operation.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-13 19:50:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.18\par
- Summary: Consolidated the new client communication-state model and synchronized the current bridge/client keepalive contract changes into the release baseline.\par
- Notes: `main/CommunicationFunctions.c`, `main/CommunicationFunctions.h`, and `main/ui_screen.c` now reflect the transport model that replaces the old `error` state with a latched `ConnectionFault` plus `wait_for_com_reset`, keeps send-data gated behind `keepalive`, and shows the reset-required connection-fault banner in the UI. The same release also preserves the client live-integer baseline across non-keepalive acknowledgements, keeps RS485 startup traffic disabled while UART2 remains future-ready, and carries the current transport-contract/documentation updates in `docs/architecture/*`. Verified through successful builds and successful flashes to `COM9` during the live bridge/client debugging cycle, with the remaining open issue still limited to bridge/server keepalive stability rather than client startup or Wi-Fi discovery.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-12 19:27:30\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.17\par
- Summary: Hardened client Wi-Fi reconnect handling so simulator reset cycles reach TCP connect and respond again.\par
- Notes: `main/CommunicationFunctions.c` now retries station association during `INITIALIZE` on a bounded timer instead of relying on a single `esp_wifi_connect()` attempt, treats `ESP_ERR_WIFI_STATE` as an in-progress association state rather than a fatal error, and skips forced disconnect/reconnect once the station already has a valid local IP. Verified with successful build, successful flash to `COM9`, and monitor capture showing the client discover `EyalSimulatorAP`, associate, obtain `192.168.4.2`, open TCP to `192.168.4.1:3333`, send `INITIALIZE` and `CONNECT`, and transition `Initialize -> Connect -> Keepalive`. The remaining live fault after this release is bridge/server-side keepalive servicing, which still times out after the client enters `KEEPALIVE`.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-12 15:19:56\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.16\par
- Summary: Disabled active RS485 startup/runtime traffic while keeping UART2 initialized for future Gaggia integration.\par
- Notes: `main/Eyal_espresso_ESP32_main.c` now skips the Gaggia controller status and version checks during startup and logs that RS485 is intentionally idle for now. `main/peripherals_manager.c` still initializes UART2/RS485 during peripheral bring-up, but the background peripheral task no longer sends RS485 heartbeat traffic. Verified with successful build, successful flash to `COM9`, and a 25-second monitor capture showing offline startup completing, the RS485 checks skipped by design, and the client returning to the main UI path while communication reconnects in the background.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-12 14:34:13\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.15\par
- Summary: Added reversible RS485 line diagnostics and hardened the wait-sound prompt workflow with persistent event logging.\par
- Notes: `main/peripherals_manager.c` now includes the temporary `ESPRESSO_RS485_DIAGNOSTICS` probe path with TX hex dumps, UART state snapshots, RX raw-buffer logging, and explicit request-write outcome logs so the controller path can be validated and later reverted cleanly. `scripts/build_flash_prompt.ps1` now starts the wait sound before `Read-Host` and always stops it afterward, while the root and duplicated `08_lvgl_Porting` sound helpers append lifecycle and playback events to `.cache/sound_events.log` for debugging missed notifications. Verified with successful host build, successful flash to `COM9`, and a bounded serial capture showing valid `INIT?\r\n` transmission plus a clean RS485 timeout with no reply bytes, which confirms the remaining controller issue is lack of remote response rather than local UART corruption.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-12 12:45:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.14\par
- Summary: Added a 5-second startup-mode countdown with Online as the default and preserved Offline as a placeholder initialization flag.\par
- Notes: `main/ui_screen.c` now shows `Offline` and `Online` buttons, updates the question text once per second with a visible countdown, and auto-selects `Online` after 5 seconds if the operator does nothing. `main/Eyal_espresso_ESP32_main.c` now normalizes the startup selection into an explicit options structure with `offline_mode_requested` carried through the initialization sequence while Wi-Fi, communication, controller handshake, and version checks still use the live server path for both startup choices. Verified with successful host reconfigure, successful host build, successful flash to `COM9`, and a 20-second post-flash monitor capture showing the client booting, associating to `EyalSimulatorAP`, obtaining `192.168.4.2`, and reaching `Connect -> Keepalive`, though the startup window still includes an existing controller-status failure and Wi-Fi warning that are not resolved by this UI change.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-12 12:25:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.13\par
- Summary: Refactored the sound notification helpers to use tracked background workers and duplicated the helper set into the `08_lvgl_Porting` demo project.\par
- Notes: `scripts/start_wait_sound.ps1`, `scripts/stop_wait_sound.ps1`, `scripts/play_wait_sound.ps1`, and `scripts/play_build_success_sound.ps1` now use `scripts/sound_process_registry.ps1` to register descriptive PID metadata for wait-loop, wait-playback, and build-success playback processes under `.cache\sound_processes`. Host-level verification showed the previous immediate worker exit was caused by sandboxed process lifetime, not the loop logic itself. The same sound-helper scripts plus the required WAV assets were duplicated into `ESP-IDF_DEMO_Files/08_lvgl_Porting`, and that project now includes its own local `VERSION` file.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-11 22:10:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.12\par
- Summary: Stabilized low-level framed transport, documented the implemented upper-level and low-level state machines, and verified reconnect behavior after Reset Connection.\par
- Notes: `main/CommunicationFunctions.c` now enlarges the framed RX buffer, clears buffered bytes instead of latching a hard error on transient overflow, logs explicit low-level error reasons, and continues using the implemented `reset -> initialize -> connect -> keepalive -> send_data -> error` transport sequence. The detailed design was expanded to describe both the upper-level application workflow state machine and the low-level communication state machine, including exact frame construction with `SOF=A55A`, little-endian length/counter/sequence fields, CRC16 coverage, keepalive ownership, and reconnect expectations. Verified with successful build, successful flash to `COM9`, and long monitor sessions showing `Connect -> Keepalive` plus successful reset-driven reconnect after the bridge-side stale-session fix.\par
\par
