- Version: 0.1.Z\par
- Summary: Fixed LVGL UI creation race by aligning mutex lock semantics with demo usage.\par
- Notes: Changed `lvgl_port_lock()` to treat `<=0` as blocking forever and updated `app_main` to call `lvgl_port_lock(-1)` before `ui_screen_create()`.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-05\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.1\par
- Summary: Display bring-up stabilized and verified working on target LCD after demo alignment and LVGL/touch/init fixes.\par
- Notes: Generated sub-version release after successful build+flash validation with functional screen output.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-05\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.1\par
- Summary: Suppressed benign GT911 startup warning in runtime logs.\par
- Notes: Set GT911 tag log level to `ESP_LOG_ERROR` in `app_main` to hide non-fatal address-init warning.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-05\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.Z\par
- Summary: Reworked UI into a workflow-style multi-page interface inspired by Gaggiuino docs patterns.\par
- Notes: Added dashboard, brew controls, profiles selection, settings tuning, bottom navigation, and live header status updates in `main/ui_screen.c`.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-05\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.Z\par
- Summary: Fixed UI compile errors by aligning font usage with enabled LVGL font set.\par
- Notes: Replaced unsupported Montserrat sizes (`18/22/24/26`) with enabled sizes (`16/20/28`) in `main/ui_screen.c`.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-06\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.2\par
- Summary: Clean build baseline release for upcoming feature and integration changes.\par
- Notes: Performed full clean, reconfigure, and successful local `idf.py build`; release created as reference baseline.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-06\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.3\par
- Summary: Fixed post-startup black-screen behavior caused by LVGL task stack overflow.\par
- Notes: Increased LVGL worker stack to 12KB, added stack watermark runtime logging, removed deprecated RGB panel union initializer overlap, and verified successful build + flash on COM9 without reboot loop.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-06\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.4\par
- Summary: Fixed periodic rightward UI drift by synchronizing LVGL framebuffer swaps to RGB panel VSYNC.\par
- Notes: Enabled tear-avoidance direct mode with panel-owned double buffers, completed flushes only on the last frame update after VSYNC notification, and verified successful local build + flash on COM9.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - DEF-20260306-180132: UI moving to the right on screen.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-07\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.5\par
- Summary: First UI-stable release with RGB bounce-buffer display path stabilized for the Waveshare 4.3B panel.\par
- Notes: Kept `psram_trans_align = 64`, enabled a 10-line RGB bounce buffer, and registered completion on `on_bounce_frame_finish`; this removed steady-state flicker and produced stable non-animation UI behavior.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - DEF-20260306-181051: Screen UI moves right every touch on screen.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-07\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.6\par
- Summary: Updated the UI to dark tab mode with swipe-driven left/right tab changes.\par
- Notes: `X` denotes major architecture or feature-set changes, `Y` denotes minor functionality additions and bug-fix milestones, and `Z` denotes accepted build+flash sub-version releases. This release keeps `X=0` and `Y=1`, and increments `Z` to capture the new tab interaction behavior in `main/ui_screen.c`.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - None in this release.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-07\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.7\par
- Summary: Added the dedicated application requirements and design document to the project.\par
- Notes: Introduced `EyalEspressoRequirements and Design.docx` as the primary requirements/design artifact and linked it from `README.md`. This remains a `Z` increment because it is a project-documentation addition rather than a major architecture or feature-scope change.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - None in this release.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-07\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.8\par
- Summary: Added TF card initialization and read verification to normal application startup.\par
- Notes: Exposed standalone TF card APIs in `main/peripherals_manager.*`, mounted and smoke-tested the card during startup from `main/Eyal_espresso_ESP32_main.c`, and fixed the SD mount CH422G mask so backlight and LCD control lines stay high during TF initialization.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - None in this release.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-07\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.9\par
- Summary: Added a startup initialization state with splash screen before the main UI loads.\par
- Notes: `main/ui_screen.c` now shows an `Initializing System...` splash for five seconds, then transitions automatically into the existing tabbed workflow UI using a one-shot LVGL timer.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - None in this release.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-07\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.10\par
- Summary: Added RTC startup initialization and fixed TF card startup verification on the Waveshare board.\par
- Notes: `main/peripherals_manager.*` now initializes the PCF85063A RTC from the current firmware build timestamp, keeps CH422G-driven SD chip select asserted for SDSPI access, allows first-mount FAT formatting, and uses an 8.3 smoke-test filename so TF mount plus read/write verification succeed during normal startup.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - None in this release.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-07\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.11\par
- Summary: Added Wi-Fi startup initialization and runtime scan verification.\par
- Notes: `main/peripherals_manager.*` now initializes NVS, `esp_netif`, the Wi-Fi station driver, and performs a blocking AP scan during startup, while `main/Eyal_espresso_ESP32_main.c` logs the result. The project flash configuration was also aligned to the board's 16MB flash with a 7MB factory app partition so the Wi-Fi-enabled firmware fits and boots cleanly.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - None in this release.\par
