\b 2026-03-08\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.4\par
- Summary: Added a Connection Info screen and refined the Settings layout into a symmetric button grid.\par
- Notes: `main/ui_screen.c` now shows `Backlight`, `Set Clock`, `Connection Info`, and `Reboot Client` as paired buttons with identical sizing, while `Connection Info` opens a scrollable overlay with IP address, controller port, and telemetry text plus a bottom `Done` button. `main/peripherals_manager.*` now exposes a connection snapshot API for the UI, including Wi-Fi IP, AP count, RTC/TF readiness, and controller status.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - None in this release.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-08\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.5\par
- Summary: Added staged initialization flow with offline/online selection, failure handling, and a System Constants viewer.\par
- Notes: `main/ui_screen.*` now starts with an `Offline Mode?` prompt, shows staged initialization progress, exposes failure-confirm and error/reset flows, and adds a Settings `System Constants` viewer plus initialization layout cleanup. `main/Eyal_espresso_ESP32_main.c` now runs a reusable staged initialization sequence with offline simulation, controller/version checks, and re-entry support. `main/peripherals_manager.*` now supports simulated connection state and controller-version requests for startup checks.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - None in this release.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-09\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.6\par
- Timestamp: 2026-03-09 14:02:36\par
- Summary: Added the low-level Wi-Fi/TCP communication module and wired `Reset Connection` into the Connection Info screen.\par
- Notes: Added `main/CommunicationFunctions.*` to own default Wi-Fi server settings, a `reset / initialize / connect / disconnect / error` state machine, TCP keep-alive progression, and a runtime snapshot API. `main/ui_screen.c` now shows a top `Reset Connection` button and live low-level communication details in the Connection Info overlay, while `main/Eyal_espresso_ESP32_main.c` initializes the communication task during staged startup. Verified with successful `idf.py build`, flash to `COM9`, and 20-second post-flash serial log capture.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - None in this release.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-09\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.7\par
- Timestamp: 2026-03-09 14:31:52\par
- Summary: Added device scanning to Connection Info and hardened the raw monitor capture script to release COM ports correctly.\par
- Notes: `main/ui_screen.c` now places `Reset Connection` and `Scan for Devices` in the standard two-column action row, switches the Connection Info text box into scan-results mode, and clears previous text immediately on scan start. `main/CommunicationFunctions.*` now includes a dedicated scan sub-state machine with `COMMUNICATION_SCAN_STATE_IDLE / REQUESTED / IN_PROGRESS / COMPLETE / ERROR`, a fixed 10-second Wi-Fi AP discovery window, and formatted result storage for the UI. `docs/architecture/*` and `docs/EyalEspressoDetailedDesign.docx` were updated to describe the scan workflow, and `scripts/monitor_capture.ps1` now explicitly closes and disposes the serial handle so COM9 is released after log capture. Verified with successful local build, direct flash to `COM9`, and a 20-second post-flash monitor run that released the port cleanly even though no serial text was emitted during that capture window.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - None in this release.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-09\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.10\par
- Timestamp: 2026-03-09 18:26:55\par
- Summary: Expanded client connection error reporting and updated the detailed design documentation for the new transport fault classifications.\par
- Notes: `main/CommunicationFunctions.c` now distinguishes configured-AP offline/not-visible failures, TCP server not found or not listening failures, and generic stage-specific transport failures. `docs/architecture/transport_contract.md`, `scripts/generate_detailed_design_docx.ps1`, and `docs/EyalEspressoDetailedDesign.docx` now document the new error mapping, including the rule that `COM port not found` is a simulator-bridge-side condition that must be reported by protocol before the client may show it as a specific diagnosis. Verified with successful local build, flash to `COM9`, and a 20-second post-flash serial log review showing the new image booting cleanly and scanning visible APs.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - None in this release.\par
